#: ../../shopify_catalog_reconciliation.md:13 a939cc63934e4b2f98a7e6de620a3d71
msgid "What it does"
msgstr ""

#: ../../shopify_catalog_reconciliation.md:15 98c8c31acee64b589492dc08ef16bc37
msgid ""
"Verifies that Shopify actually reflects what Airtable says should be "
"sellable, in three checks, from broad to specific:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../shopify_catalog_reconciliation.md:18 7a1e9f69569a4da29d202f79f7a05b45
msgid "**Every relevant Model exists as a Shopify product.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../shopify_catalog_reconciliation.md:19 51eb8b3a1d51400a820b980ec1f1dc6f
msgid ""
"**Every relevant Variation of a Model found in Shopify exists as a "
"Shopify variant.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../shopify_catalog_reconciliation.md:20 9d8206cd830741f888a4b4ae5b5a1be7
msgid ""
"**Every \"A vendre\" unit's Shopify variant has the right inventory "
"quantity.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../shopify_catalog_reconciliation.md:22 74a41db359b44a46b8bc0ab710f03ef9
msgid ""
"\"Relevant\" always means: flagged `to_sell_on_shopify` **and** currently"
" has at least one unit in stock (`Statut commercial = \"A vendre\"`). A "
"Model or Variation that's the *kind* of thing sold online but has zero "
"stock right now is correctly absent from Shopify -- it is never flagged "
"as \"missing\". Units in an excluded condition (`EXCLUDED_CONDITIONS`: "
"\"Abimé\", \"Très abimé\", compared ignoring accents and case) are never "
"put on Shopify by `create_product_shopify`/`update_product`, so they "
"don't count as stock here either."
msgstr ""

#: ../../shopify_catalog_reconciliation.md:29 4a389dfce8cb4883aa40a79c963f1def
msgid "It also reports catalog integrity problems, outside those three checks:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../shopify_catalog_reconciliation.md:31 d39f72b12806485a9360b3e9561ff80b
msgid ""
"**Prices at 0** on either side. These are A vendre units expected on "
"Shopify whose `Prix de vente HT` is 0, empty or invalid; "
"`create_product_shopify` and `update_product` refuse to run on such a "
"Model. It also reports Shopify variants priced at 0 that Airtable still "
"has A vendre units for (same Variation and condition), on a product that "
"isn't archived, since those are meant to be sold. A 0 € variant with no A"
" vendre stock in Airtable is correct: the sales team sets the price to 0 "
"when stock runs out."
msgstr ""

#: ../../shopify_catalog_reconciliation.md:38 01bfe4f8d9fa40848f3e45dbe629595a
msgid ""
"**Duplicates and orphans**, which break \"one Model = one Annonces "
"Shopify = one Shopify product\":"
msgstr ""

#: ../../shopify_catalog_reconciliation.md:40 f4bed5bed22b4ddea03c455e55f53350
msgid ""
"Shopify products with the same title, e.g. a creation that ran twice. "
"Each copy shows which Model it belongs to, or none. Different products "
"can share a name, so a group is only reported when a copy belongs to no "
"Model or two copies belong to the same Model. Same-title products that "
"each have their own Model and Annonces Shopify are correct."
msgstr ""

#: ../../shopify_catalog_reconciliation.md:45 12f0dcdbf04549b483aab31b75853c6e
msgid ""
"Shopify products that no Annonces Shopify record and no Model refers to, "
"except drafts (being prepared, not orderable yet). This one is "
"**informational, not an error**: some products legitimately exist only on"
" Shopify, and the dashboard lists them (neutral style, low priority) so "
"they can be identified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../shopify_catalog_reconciliation.md:49 a9f132238e66435cb1e18610b16ef7ea
msgid "Models linked to more than one Annonces Shopify record."
msgstr ""

#: ../../shopify_catalog_reconciliation.md:50 af82187e7d874e5b9ca0987e87e46537
msgid "Shopify ids used by more than one Annonces Shopify record."
msgstr ""

#: ../../shopify_catalog_reconciliation.md:51 294361b5e3a949bb9a9ad276a442059e
msgid ""
"Units not yet sold whose Variation(s) lead to more than one listing, for "
"example through a Model with two listings, or a unit linked to Variations"
" of two Models."
msgstr ""

#: ../../shopify_catalog_reconciliation.md:54 c0cf2d3e80f34c4d8a83014e602b30b6
msgid ""
"These are reports only: the run stays `success`, and the script still "
"changes nothing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../shopify_catalog_reconciliation.md:56 c653977732dc438791309973d5b372f2
msgid "Why the matching is value-based, not ID-based"
msgstr ""

#: ../../shopify_catalog_reconciliation.md:58 60dd035558cb4675b6bcf7a19dc1022e
msgid ""
"Airtable's `Variation.ShopifyID` field is **not a real variant id** -- "
"confirmed against production data, it always duplicates the parent "
"Model's own product id, even across Variations that are genuinely "
"different Shopify variants. There is no Airtable field holding a real "
"Shopify variant id at all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../shopify_catalog_reconciliation.md:63 3bba8a0d56274a59b28cd857ebd6e10b
msgid ""
"Instead, a Shopify variant is identified by its `selectedOptions` "
"**values** (the option *names* vary per product type -- a pipette's size "
"option isn't named the same as a fridge's -- so matching is name-"
"agnostic, value-only). Those literal value strings match Airtable, once "
"both sides are whitespace-normalized:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../shopify_catalog_reconciliation.md:68 a97c8d4e3b7b4eb086e7406a6175575d
msgid "a Variation's own `Variant_value` (a size/range, e.g. `\"5 - 50\"`), plus"
msgstr ""

#: ../../shopify_catalog_reconciliation.md:69 3d6f304e60ee414189737ddd761bfe9c
msgid "a Unit's own `Etat esthétique` (condition, e.g. `\"Très bon\"`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../shopify_catalog_reconciliation.md:71 8c57afbde45e4881b57a675564e528cf
msgid ""
"...together pin down exactly one Shopify variant. So **one Airtable "
"Variation corresponds to one Shopify variant *per condition it currently "
"has stock in***, not a single variant -- and a unit that's \"A vendre\" "
"through a different channel entirely (eBay, an auction, direct sale) is "
"never expected on Shopify in the first place, so it's excluded from all "
"three checks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../shopify_catalog_reconciliation.md:77 e204f08f577f4690b39280ad2dd4470a
#, python-format
msgid ""
"This was two real, confirmed production bugs (ID-based matching finding "
"100% of variations \"missing\"; then a scoping bug over-flagging units "
"sold through other channels) before this design -- and a third since: "
"`Variant_value` is manually-entered free text and can carry incidental "
"whitespace (a real `\"150x75 \"` in Airtable) that Shopify itself trims "
"on save (`\"150x75\"`); comparing the raw, un-normalized values meant a "
"genuinely-existing variant was reported as missing. Both "
"`Variation.variant_values` (`api/domain/catalog.py`) and "
"`ShopifyVariant.option_values` (`api/integrations/shopify.py`) now strip "
"before comparing -- the exact same class of bug independently found and "
"fixed in `update_product.py`'s own (separate) variant matching, see "
"`docs/update_product.md`."
msgstr ""

