#: ../../shopify_catalog_reconciliation.md:183 69397f52cfa04290980cf581d0280b41
msgid ""
"`details` in the same response carries the actual named records behind "
"each count above (model/variation id + name + an Airtable web-UI link via"
" `record_url`), uncapped -- the frontend acts on these lists directly (a "
"per-model \"create on Shopify\" button, and one that bulk-creates every "
"missing model), so silently dropping entries past some cap would mean "
"those specific models could never be created via the dashboard at all, "
"not just a display inconvenience."
msgstr ""

#: ../../shopify_catalog_reconciliation.md:190 87d053db7f2f49688e3c00f7b6a5ecac
msgid ""
"`attach_creation_attempts` (called from `run()`, right after "
"`attach_airtable_urls`) then cross-references each "
"`models_missing_in_shopify` entry against `create_product_shopify`'s own "
"run history (via `RunStore`, ~1000 runs kept -- see "
"`docs/architecture.rst`), and adds `entry[\"last_creation_attempt\"]` "
"(`status`, `error`, `skipped_reason`, `finished_at`) when that Model has "
"already been attempted. A Model showing up as \"missing\" isn't "
"necessarily untried -- it might already be failing for a knowable reason "
"(bad Airtable data, a stale Shopify desync, an image upload conflict), "
"and that's a very different situation from \"nobody has tried creating it"
" yet\". This is a read-only lookup against Redis (a second script's "
"stored history, not a mutation of anything) and, like "
"`attach_airtable_urls`, is wrapped so it can never fail the "
"reconciliation run itself -- a broken/unreachable RunStore just means no "
"entry gets `last_creation_attempt`, not a failed run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../shopify_catalog_reconciliation.md:203 f83d5e46815d4535a41cf2c9b83c8c94
msgid ""
"`attach_update_attempts` does the same for "
"`variations_missing_in_shopify`: each entry gets `last_update_attempt` "
"(`status`, `error`, `finished_at`) from the latest `update_product` run "
"whose `details.record_id` is that Variation. Runs triggered with "
"`model_id` have no `record_id`, so they aren't attributed to individual "
"Variations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../shopify_catalog_reconciliation.md:208 0ab85d2fecf84c28baf0b0f220ba4a70
msgid ""
"The documentation lists only cover *relevant* Models that were found on "
"Shopify (a Model missing from Shopify entirely is already "
"`models_missing_in_shopify`). The Shopify side comes from the same bulk "
"GraphQL read (two aliased `metafield(...)` fields per product). "
"`attach_documentation_attempts` adds `last_update_attempt` to the "
"missing/outdated entries from `update_product`'s history, matched by "
"`details.model_id`. It only counts runs that actually tried a "
"documentation sync (a failure, a skip, or a success with "
"`documentation_status: \"uploaded\"`). The dashboard's \"Envoyer toutes "
"les documentations manquantes\" / \"Remplacer toutes les documentations "
"obsolètes\" buttons fan out `update_product?model_id=...` over those "
"lists, 3 at a time. A run counts as updated only when it actually "
"uploaded a PDF."
msgstr ""

#: ../../shopify_catalog_reconciliation.md:219 502854b281d54822bbda6f9e3c65375c
msgid ""
"The Shopify-side entries (`shopify_variants_without_price`, "
"`duplicate_shopify_products`, `shopify_products_not_in_airtable`, and the"
" `product` of `shopify_ids_with_multiple_listings`) carry the product's "
"Shopify admin `url`. The Airtable-side ones get the record's `url` from "
"`attach_airtable_urls`, and every listing in a `listings` list gets the "
"Annonces Shopify record's `url`. The title comparison runs against the "
"whole Shopify catalog; same-title products that each belong to a "
"different Model are not reported."
msgstr ""

